s own **subject and verb**.","**Because** introduces the reason as a finite clause: we had ... .","Choose **because**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"**Because** introduces the reason as a finite clause: we had ... .","B":"Because of normally takes a noun phrase or -ing expression, not this finite clause.","C":"Despite would need a noun phrase and would express contrast, not the stated reason.","D":"During takes a noun phrase, not a finite clause."}}},{"id":"0167808b-04f3-5abc-ab94-3af742b723d0","topicSlug":"linking-clauses","level":"B1","prompt":"“We could not measure the garden fence ____ the power cut.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"because of"},{"id":"B","text":"because"},{"id":"C","text":"although"},{"id":"D","text":"while"}],"answerId":"A","hint":"The reason is a **noun phrase**, so choose because of.","explanation":"The reason is a noun phrase, **the power cut**, so use **because of**.","keywords":["because-of-noun"],"skill":"because-of-noun","contextKey":"linking-clauses-3","fingerprint":"040d838858354eee24d4d7338576166fbfefbbb167fb0195787ee892ad8b8c9e","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["dfe-grammar"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["The reason is a **noun phrase**, so choose because of.","The reason is a noun phrase, **the power cut**, so use **because of**.","Choose **because of**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"The reason is a noun phrase, **the power cut**, so use **because of**.","B":"Because requires a finite reason clause rather than this noun phrase alone.","C":"Although normally introduces a finite clause and gives contrast rather than this reason.","D":"While would normally introduce a clause, not this bare reason phrase."}}},{"id":"9309dd00-bf13-5aa3-a98f-4ff21ad51444","topicSlug":"linking-clauses","level":"B1","prompt":"Express purpose with a different subject: “I brought the instructions ____ you could measure the garden fence.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"so that"},{"id":"B","text":"in order to"},{"id":"C","text":"because of"},{"id":"D","text":"despite"}],"answerId":"A","hint":"The purpose clause has its own subject **you** and modal **could**.","explanation":"**So that** introduces a finite purpose clause whose subject is you.","keywords":["purpose-so-that"],"skill":"purpose-so-that","contextKey":"linking-clauses-3","fingerprint":"4e5ca5a8443810013c0856932310dc213e2c10176a3977e0a3e0dae1db291e41","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["dfe-grammar"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["The purpose clause has its own subject **you** and modal **could**.","**So that** introduces a finite purpose clause whose subject is you.","Choose **so that**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"**So that** introduces a finite purpose clause whose subject is you.","B":"In order to needs a base verb immediately, not you could.","C":"Because of cannot introduce this finite purpose clause.","D":"Despite both changes the relation and requires a different complement."}}},{"id":"c57214f1-6277-54c2-a1f3-1405e667264c","topicSlug":"linking-clauses","level":"B1","prompt":"Use the time preposition before an -ing noun phrase: “The error occurred during the process of ____ the garden fence.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"to measure"},{"id":"B","text":"measured"},{"id":"C","text":"measuring"},{"id":"D","text":"measure"}],"answerId":"C","hint":"The preposition **of** needs a noun-like complement: use the **-ing form**.","explanation":"After preposition **of**, use **measuring** to name the process.","keywords":["during-while"],"skill":"during-while","contextKey":"linking-clauses-