 would need a noun phrase and would express contrast, not the stated reason.","C":"During takes a noun phrase, not a finite clause.","D":"**Because** introduces the reason as a finite clause: we had ... ."}}},{"id":"a0170bda-0e6d-50f5-ab5d-5a73de026616","topicSlug":"linking-clauses","level":"B1","prompt":"“We could not translate the travel leaflet ____ the power cut.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"although"},{"id":"B","text":"while"},{"id":"C","text":"because of"},{"id":"D","text":"because"}],"answerId":"C","hint":"The reason is a **noun phrase**, so choose because of.","explanation":"The reason is a noun phrase, **the power cut**, so use **because of**.","keywords":["because-of-noun"],"skill":"because-of-noun","contextKey":"linking-clauses-4","fingerprint":"1b99974ff1e62fd09cd97a666654b1bb14e4c8a03bd0ca35aedad29b2f790d6a","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["dfe-grammar"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["The reason is a **noun phrase**, so choose because of.","The reason is a noun phrase, **the power cut**, so use **because of**.","Choose **because of**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Although normally introduces a finite clause and gives contrast rather than this reason.","B":"While would normally introduce a clause, not this bare reason phrase.","C":"The reason is a noun phrase, **the power cut**, so use **because of**.","D":"Because requires a finite reason clause rather than this noun phrase alone."}}},{"id":"3c1ba408-88c9-5f94-a16c-1ae49b42bd57","topicSlug":"linking-clauses","level":"B1","prompt":"Express purpose with a different subject: “I brought the instructions ____ you could translate the travel leaflet.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"so that"},{"id":"B","text":"in order to"},{"id":"C","text":"because of"},{"id":"D","text":"despite"}],"answerId":"A","hint":"T